opensync-lab: DENY_ACL ADD_MAC blocks new associations only.

hostapd disassociates a station as soon as it is added to the deny list. owm's
steering blocks use OSW's hostap ACL (OSW_DRV_NL80211_ACL_IMPL_HOSTAP), and its
executor assumes a block leaves an associated station in place: it applies the
block, then sends the BTM request, then deauthenticates if the station stays.
With stock hostapd the station is gone before the BTM request, so client
steering could only ever disconnect.

--- a/hostapd/ctrl_iface.c
+++ b/hostapd/ctrl_iface.c
@@ -3556,8 +3556,7 @@ static int hostapd_ctrl_iface_receive_process(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 			if (hostapd_ctrl_iface_acl_add_mac(
 				    &hapd->conf->deny_mac,
 				    &hapd->conf->num_deny_mac, buf + 17) ||
-			    hostapd_set_acl(hapd) ||
-			    hostapd_disassoc_deny_mac(hapd))
+			    hostapd_set_acl(hapd))
 				reply_len = -1;
 		} else if (os_strncmp(buf + 9, "DEL_MAC ", 8) == 0) {
 			if (hostapd_ctrl_iface_acl_del_mac(
